A||||4||Gokart||Which bushings first?||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||02-07-2000||09:03 PM||||Beginning to notice I'm not taking bumps in the road as well as I have recently and suspect it's time for new bushings. I'd like to purchase the whole set of poly bushings from the Fiero Store but funds won't allow that. Which ones would any of you that have changed them should I do first? Which ones usually go first? TIA for replys.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||02-07-2000||10:27 PM||||Order your bushings from Suspension Restorations, I cant find the web link right now, but somebody will (hopefully!) They were the same Prothane bushings, but cost was A LOT LESS than Fiero Store. The guy was super nice and helpful. I have already put the rear bushings in my 88GT and it made a world of difference. Before the bushings, it would torque steer really bad, but now accelerates nice and straight.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||02-08-2000||01:56 AM||||I would say replace the front end first, since you have bushings in the top and bottom control arms, and the sway bar bushings and end links.  Of course, start out with what you can afford  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
